ADVISORY

A1. scripts/host-cells.mjs:64-65 — the builder cell re-derives two bind sources instead of being handed them.
builderCell computes join(runtime, "tools") and join(runtime, "control") itself, while the runner's own
`tools` (run-builder-host.mjs:564) and `controlDir` (:531) are the paths it actually copies the probe into and
hands to openCellChannel. The two spellings are equal today, so nothing is weakened and W-132's pipes are
bound correctly; the cost is that they are now independent and no source-level row pins them equal — behaviour
5 pins the imports, the call shape and the absence of the old inline code, not the arguments. A rename on
either side is caught only by the live rows, which skip where bwrap or the broker is unusable. Passing
controlDir and tools in the paths object, as `clone`, `runtime` and `etc` already are, removes the class.
Class enumeration, and what I searched: every `join(runtime,` in host-cells.mjs and every bind source in the
runner's three cells — exactly two instances, both at this call site; the replay cell and the gate cell
re-derive nothing.

A2. scripts/run-builder-host.mjs:764 — replay preparation leaves npm state in the private HOME the replay then
runs in. The runner creates /home/builder empty at :754 and the brief's reconciliation says the build runs in
"the same private HOME/tmp"; it does, but it runs first. Measured here on a clean HOME with the fixed argv
(probe-replay-home-pollution.sh, npm-home-probe.log): `npm --workspace @bisellium/web run build` leaves
~/.npm/_logs/<ts>-debug-0.log. So for any checkout carrying apps/web/package.json — which is every commit of
this repo, i.e. all five of W-130's own reds — the recorded command no longer starts against the pristine home
W-125 gave it. No confinement consequence: the home is private, unreadable from the host and torn down with
the cell, and the receipt shows all five reds still reproduce. The gap is that the replay's starting state
changed without being stated or asserted in either direction, so a future red that counts or asserts on HOME
would be decided by whether its checkout happens to carry a web workspace. One instance: the build is the only
command newly introduced into a cell by this opus (the runner's other cell launches are unchanged).

DECLARED DEVIATION — accepted.
packages/commands/src/run.test.ts:1237, the W-132-b1 live-row census, 19 -> 26. The assertion postdates the
brief, and the brief's catch-all in Files owned authorises edits to rows that pin "the runner's cell shape,
